      "title": "Reentrancy in withdraw allows full vault drain",
      "severity": "critical",
      "description": "The `withdraw` function transfers Ether to `msg.sender` using a low-level `.call` before decrementing the caller's balance. Because the balance is updated after the external call, a malicious recipient can reenter `withdraw` recursively and withdraw far more than its recorded balance.",
      "evidence": {
